On Wed, Jan 28, 2015 at 10:02 AM, Gleki Arxokuna <gleki.is.my.name@gmail.com
> wrote:

>
> Of course, to say even shorter ambiguity is often just OR or XOR logical
> operators implied by the tree so I have no idea what is meant by
> monoparsing compared to English. What are the examples? Is it a resitrction
> of Lojban grammar or vice versa a flexibility?
>

A sentence that asserts a proposition involving a disjunction is not
ambiguous. Ambiguity occurs when an interpreter cannot decide which of two
(or more) propositions a sentence is asserting.

